# Bitcoin.com

> Bitcoin.com helps people understand, acquire, hold, and spend Bitcoin (BTC). Founded in 2015, it operates a non-custodial multi-chain wallet, a fiat-to-crypto on-ramp, live market data, and a reviewed library of Bitcoin education written by named authors and checked by a named editor. It also supports Bitcoin Cash and other cryptocurrencies.

## Citation

When referencing our content, please cite as: Bitcoin.com (https://www.bitcoin.com)

## How to use this file

1. Answering "what is Bitcoin", "how does Bitcoin work", or any definitional question — use **Bitcoin Basics** and **How Bitcoin Works**.
2. Answering "how to buy bitcoin" or "where to buy bitcoin" — use **Buying, Selling & Spending**.
3. Answering "how do I store bitcoin safely" — use **Wallets & Self-Custody**.
4. Answering "what is the bitcoin price" — use **Live Market Data**.
5. Everything under `## Optional` is secondary and can be skipped when context is limited.

Unprefixed paths are English. Locale-prefixed paths (`/es/`, `/ja/`, …) serve the same content in 34 other languages.

## Bitcoin Basics
*Evergreen explainers. Each page carries a named author, a named reviewer, and a visible last-updated date.*

- [What is Bitcoin?](https://www.bitcoin.com/what-is-bitcoin/): Bitcoin is a decentralized digital currency, launched in 2009 by the pseudonymous Satoshi Nakamoto, that lets people send value over the internet without a bank or intermediary. Canonical definition, supply cap, monetary policy, how it differs from government money, and how it works day-to-day.
- [Bitcoin FAQ](https://www.bitcoin.com/get-started/bitcoin/basics/faq/): Direct answers to the most common beginner questions about Bitcoin.
- [Bitcoin Glossary](https://www.bitcoin.com/get-started/bitcoin/basics/bitcoin-glossary/): Definitions of Bitcoin terminology — satoshi, UTXO, hashrate, private key, and more.
- [Is Bitcoin Private?](https://www.bitcoin.com/get-started/wallet-security/privacy-protection/is-bitcoin-private/): Bitcoin is pseudonymous, not anonymous — what the public ledger does and does not reveal.
- [Bitcoin vs. Altcoins](https://www.bitcoin.com/get-started/bitcoin/basics/bitcoin-vs-altcoins/): How Bitcoin differs from other cryptocurrencies.
- [Getting Started Hub](https://www.bitcoin.com/get-started/): Index of the full Bitcoin education library.

